<title>USA: Faulding gets tentative okay for drug.</title>
<headline>Faulding gets tentative okay for drug.</headline>
<dateline>ELIZABETH, N.J. 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Faulding Inc's Purepac Pharmaceutical Co said on Tuesday that it has received tentative approval from the Food and Drug Administration to manufacture and market etodolac tablets, a generic version of Lodine.</p>
<p>Lodine, a product made by the Wyeth-Ayerst unit of American Home Products Corp, is indicated for acute and long term use in the management of osteoarthritis and pain, the company said.</p>
<p>Final FDA approval is expected upon expiration of the brand's patent on February 28, 1997, the company said.</p>
</text>
